A regression probe run over 2 of the 3 classified documents of this corpus.

## The run identity this plan fixes

```yaml
lock: sha256:ca3c47a2f8b062bab1b62b6f5849be25b89110ec578b22da01968aa51148c4c7
tree: sha256:f445be2bee480bd419137a84965ce7f5bffe67a3335819be0e41fd1bebb1878d
selection: sha256:f42c669753dc4e211eaee04b9d79b8fb0f78499300923e1341f815bb5a5ce0af
read_set: sha256:ac1e3801b1f468f6fb03496ce0698d4d1a5a083a6424e6d2050846daaa2acc48
seed: 0
harness: 0.8.3
tier: regression
arms: [present]
```

The model, its served version, the wall-clock time and the realized cost belong to the run. The recorder writes those four into the transcript, and `headwater probe record` holds the rest of the identity to the six above.

## The cost

2 probes x 1 arms x 1 repetitions = 2 sessions, at a declared $0.25 each: $0.50 against a ceiling of $20.00.
The unit cost is a number a person declared in `.headwater/probe.yml`. No run has happened, so no realized cost has been recorded against it and this is arithmetic rather than a forecast.

